==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From [[lenis]] + ''-ition'' (modelled on German [[Lenierung]]).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/liːˈnɪʃən/|/ləˈnɪʃən/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|linguistics|lang=en}} A weakening of [[articulation]] causing a consonant to become [[lenis]] ([[soft]]).

====Antonyms====
* [[fortition]]

